WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.403
The goal of dataset distillation is to shrink a big
dataset into a small synthetic set that still trains models well.

00:00:07.483 --> 00:00:11.497
Most existing work pours its energy into the
matching objective,

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:14.887
the loss that aligns the synthetic and real datasets.

00:00:14.967 --> 00:00:20.068
But how the synthetic images are actually
parameterized has been an afterthought.

00:00:20.148 --> 00:00:24.353
The standard approach optimizes each synthetic
image independently,

00:00:24.433 --> 00:00:31.197
a naive scheme that never exploits the fact that
natural images share enormous amounts of visual structure,

00:00:31.277 --> 00:00:34.715
both within a single image and across different images.

00:00:34.795 --> 00:00:39.320
This spatial redundancy silently wastes the already
tiny storage budget,

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.710
and the problem gets worse as image resolution grows.
